8. Room Card Design
The Merged Room Card
Each room card is a composite of two data sources:
Website content (Layer 1): Presentation content, descriptions, amenities, highlights, bed type, area, and any media the website provides
InnPilot data (Layer 2): Availability, nightly rate, stay total, packages, available room count
The card renders Layer 1 immediately. Layer 2 populates after the API responds. If the API is slow, the card shows the room's content with a "Checking availability…" state in the pricing area.
Progressive Enhancement: Presentation Assets
The room card is designed to be fully functional without any presentation assets. Every visual element — images, galleries, videos, decorative photography — is a progressive enhancement layered on top of a complete, bookable room card.
Without presentation assets, a room card shows:
- Room name (from website content, or from API as fallback)
- Short description (from website content)
- Occupancy, bed type, area (from website content)
- Amenities (from website content)
- Pricing and availability (from InnPilot API)
- Package options (from InnPilot API)
- Select button (functional)
- All of the above are operational and complete
With presentation assets, a room card additionally shows:
- Whatever media the website's presentation layer provides
The absence of presentation assets does not leave a broken placeholder. The card adapts its layout to accommodate the missing content gracefully. This is not a degraded experience — it is a different, equally valid layout.
Data Source Labels
For implementation clarity, every element in the room card is tagged with its source:
Element Source  Dependency  Notes
Presentation area Website content Enhancement Absent → card adapts to compact layout
Room name Website content (primary) / InnPilot API (fallback) Critical  Always displayed; source varies
Short description Website content Enhancement Absent → card omits description, remains functional
Occupancy (max) Website content Enhancement Absent → omitted from info grid
Bed type  Website content Enhancement Absent → omitted from info grid
Room area Website content Enhancement Absent → omitted from info grid
Amenities Website content Enhancement Absent → amenities section omitted
Highlights  Website content Enhancement Absent → highlights omitted
Nightly rate  InnPilot API  Critical  Always displayed after API response
Stay total  InnPilot API  Critical  Always displayed after API response
Original total (if discounted)  InnPilot API  Critical  For strikethrough display
Available rooms count InnPilot API  Critical  Always displayed after API response
Packages  InnPilot API  Critical  Always displayed after API response
Package pricing InnPilot API  Critical  Always displayed after API response
Select button Functional  Critical  Always rendered; disabled if unavailable
Room Card States
State Visual Treatment
Content loaded, API pending Full content visible (or compact if no presentation assets), pricing area shows skeleton shimmer with "Checking availability…"
Available Full colour, normal shadow, standard border, pricing populated
Selected  Green accent border (2px), subtle green background tint, "Selected ✓" badge replaces Select button
Unavailable Content still visible (description, amenities), pricing area shows "Not available for these dates", select button disabled and grey
Sold out  Content visible, "Sold Out" overlay or badge (if presentation area exists), greyed-out select button, opacity 0.6
Hover Slight elevation increase (shadow-glow), border brightens
Comparing Checkbox in top-right checked, subtle highlight
The Graceful Degradation Principle
The room card has three possible degradation scenarios. In every case, the booking flow remains functional.
Scenario 1: InnPilot API unreachable
- Room content still renders (website content)
- Pricing area shows "Unable to check availability. Please try again."
- The "Check Availability" button in the search bar retries the API call
- The page is never blank. Content is always visible.
Scenario 2: No presentation assets (no images, no galleries, no videos)
- Room name displayed (from website content, or from API as fallback)
- Pricing and availability from API still function
- Select button works normally
- The card layout adapts to be compact (no presentation area)
- The booking flow is fully functional. The experience is less visually rich but operationally complete.
Scenario 3: Both degraded (no API + no presentation assets)
- Room names displayed (from API if available, otherwise from website content)
- Pricing shows "Unable to check availability"
- Select button is disabled
- The page shows room names and structure but cannot complete bookings
- This is an extreme edge case. The retry mechanism and error states guide the user.
Room Info Grid
A compact 3–4 column info strip below the description. Each element is independently optional:
Icon  Field Source  Example If Missing
Occupancy Adults + Children Website content "2 Adults + 1 Child"  Chip omitted
Bed Bed type  Website content "King Bed"  Chip omitted
Area  Room area Website content "450 sq ft" Chip omitted
Highlight Best included package InnPilot API  "Jungle Safari Included"  Chip omitted (or API not yet loaded)
The info grid only renders chips for data that exists. It never shows empty or placeholder chips.
Amenities Display
- Source: Website content layer
- Shown as pill/chip elements
- Max 6 visible, "+X more" overflow
- Tap to expand full list
- Progressive enhancement: If no amenities are defined for a room, the amenities section is entirely omitted from the card. No "No amenities listed" placeholder.
Pricing Display
- Source: InnPilot API exclusively
Two lines:
1. Per night: ₹7,000 / night — large, bold
2. Stay total: ₹21,000 for 3 nights (Jul 25 – Jul 28) — smaller, lighter
If a discount applies:
3. Original: ₹25,000 — strikethrough
4. Discounted: ₹21,000 — green, with "Save ₹4,000" badge
The total is what the API returns for the given dates. The frontend does not calculate.
9. Package Selection Design
Source: InnPilot API
Packages appear within the room card after the user taps "Select This Room" or expands the packages section. Package data comes entirely from InnPilot. The website does not define or override packages.
Package Tiers
The API returns packages with tier/status information. The frontend renders them with clear visual differentiation:
Tier  Visual  Badge
Included  Checkbox checked, green, disabled (cannot uncheck)  "Included" — green pill
Optional  Checkbox unchecked, tappable  Price shown as "+₹X,XXX"
Recommended Checkbox unchecked, highlighted with subtle border, "Recommended" badge "Recommended" — gold pill
Unavailable Greyed out, strikethrough, "Sold Out" label "Sold Out" — grey pill
