Design notes:
- Warm, not apologetic
- Offer an alternative path (search again, contact directly)
- Do not show an empty list
- Website content (hero, page styling) remains visible — only the rooms section is empty
Initial State (No Search Performed)
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                              │
│  Enter your travel dates to discover         │
│  available rooms at Corbett Foothills.       │
│                                              │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │       [ Check Availability ]         │    │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────┘    │
│                                              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
Design notes:
- Do not show empty room slots
- Do not show a blank page
- Guide the user toward the search bar
- The page's visual richness (hero, typography, colour) is entirely website content — it renders before any API call
API Unreachable
If the InnPilot API is unreachable when the user searches:
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                              │
│  We're having trouble checking availability. │
│                                              │
│  This is temporary. Please try again in      │
│  a moment.                                   │
│                                              │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │          [ Try Again ]               │    │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────┘    │
│                                              │
│  Or contact us directly:                     │
│  📞 +91 98181 93314                          │
│  💬 WhatsApp                                 │
│                                              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
Design notes:
- The page's visual framework (header, hero, footer, trust signals) remains fully rendered — only the rooms section shows the error
- This is the key benefit of the two-layer architecture: content and operations degrade independently
Room Content Missing (Slug Mismatch)
If the InnPilot API returns a room slug that has no matching website content:
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                              │
│  [Room Name from API]                        │
│  (compact layout — no presentation area)     │
│                                              │
│  Details for this room are being prepared.   │
│                                              │
│  ₹X,XXX / night                             │
│  (innpilot pricing — fully functional)       │
│                                              │
│  [ Select This Room ]                       │
│  (operational — booking works normally)      │
│                                              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
Design notes:
- The card still functions — the user can still select and book
- No placeholder presentation area. The card uses the compact layout.
- The name comes from the API
- A brief "Details being prepared" note indicates content is forthcoming
- Pricing and booking still work normally
- This is a graceful degradation, not an error
Presentation Assets Partially Available
A room may have some content but not others. The card renders whatever exists:
Content Available Card Shows
Name + description + amenities + presentation assets  Full enhanced card
Name + description + amenities (no presentation assets) Compact card with text content
Name + presentation assets (no description) Card with presentation area, no description block
Name only (no other content)  Minimal card with name, pricing, and select button
Nothing (API slug only) Minimal card with API name, pricing, and select button
In every case, the card is functional. The booking flow works. The user can always select a room, see pricing, and complete a booking.
12. Loading States
Search Loading
When the user taps "Check Availability," the rooms section transitions to a skeleton state:
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                              │
│  [Skeleton card 1]                           │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │ ████████████████████████████████████  │    │
│  │ ████  ████████████████████████████   │    │
│  │ ████  ████████████████               │    │
│  │ ████  ██████████████                 │    │
│  │ ████  ████████████████████████████   │    │
│  │ ████████████████████████████████████  │    │
│  │         [ ████████████████ ]         │    │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────┘    │
│                                              │
│  [Skeleton card 2]                           │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │ ████████████████████████████████████  │    │
│  │ ████  ████████████████████████████   │    │
│  │ ████  ████████████████               │    │
│  │ ████  ██████████████                 │    │
│  │ ████  ████████████████████████████   │    │
│  │ ████████████████████████████████████  │    │
│  │         [ ████████████████ ]         │    │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────┘    │
│                                              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
Design notes:
- Skeleton cards match the exact dimensions of real room cards
- Shimmer animation (subtle, left-to-right gradient)
- 2–3 skeleton cards shown (not more)
- Loading text: "Finding available rooms…" — small, below search bar
- In practice, website content loads almost instantly (static/CDN), so the skeleton primarily covers the API response time
Progressive Loading Pattern
The ideal loading sequence is:
1. 0ms: Page frame renders (header, hero, search bar, footer) — website content
2. 0–100ms: Room cards render with website content (descriptions, amenities, and any presentation assets) — website content
3. 100–500ms: API responds with availability and pricing — InnPilot data
4. 500ms: Pricing areas in room cards populate, summary updates
This means the user sees room content almost immediately. The "loading" experience is limited to the pricing areas, not the entire card. This is a direct benefit of the two-layer architecture.
If presentation assets are missing: The loading sequence is even faster because there are fewer assets to render in step 2. The cards appear in their compact layout immediately, with pricing populating in step 3–4.
Summary Loading
When a room is selected and the quote is being fetched:
- Summary price lines show skeleton shimmer
- CTA button shows "Loading…" and is disabled
- Room selection remains visible (website content is already loaded)
- Room name and dates are already populated (user selection + website content)
