Booking Error
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                              │
│  We couldn't complete your booking.          │
│  Don't worry — you haven't been charged.     │
│                                              │
│  Reason: [API error message]                 │
│                                              │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │        [ Try Again ]                 │    │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────┘    │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │     [ Contact Us Instead ]           │    │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────┘    │
│                                              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
Quote Error (Package Change Failed)
If updating packages fails when calling /quote:
- The package selection reverts to the previous state
- A subtle toast message appears: "Unable to update packages. Please try again."
- The user's room selection is preserved
- No data is lost
Field Validation Errors
- Inline, below the field
- Red text, small, with subtle icon
- Field border turns red
- Error appears on blur, not on every keystroke
- Error disappears when corrected
┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│ Email                            │
│ not-a-valid-email                │ ← red text below
└──────────────────────────────────┘
Room No Longer Available
If a room becomes unavailable between selection and booking (the API returns updated availability during the booking flow):
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ⚠ This room is no longer available for      │
│    your selected dates.                       │
│                                              │
│  Please select another room or adjust         │
│  your dates.                                 │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
Design note: The room's website content remains visible. Only the availability status has changed. The card shifts to the "unavailable" state.
Content Layer Unreachable
If the website's own content layer (CMS or markdown files) fails to load room content:
- Room cards render with API data only (name, pricing, availability)
- No descriptions, no amenities from website content
- Cards use the compact layout
- The booking flow is fully functional. The user can still see availability, pricing, and complete a booking.
- This scenario is unlikely with static site builds (content is baked in) but possible with a headless CMS
14. API Interaction Flow
Sequence Diagram
User              Frontend             Website Content       InnPilot API
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │  Page load        │                      │                    │
 │──────────────────→│                      │                    │
 │                   │  Load room content   │                    │
 │                   │  (markdown/CMS)      │                    │
 │                   │─────────────────────→│                    │
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │                   │  { rooms: [...] }    │                    │
 │                   │  text content,       │                    │
 │                   │  presentation*       │  (* = optional)    │
 │                   │←─────────────────────│                    │
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │  Show room cards  │                      │                    │
 │  (content, or     │                      │                    │
 │   compact if      │                      │                    │
 │   no assets)      │                      │                    │
 │←──────────────────│                      │                    │
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │  Enter dates,     │                      │                    │
 │  Tap "Search"     │                      │                    │
 │──────────────────→│                      │                    │
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │                   │  GET /availability   │                    │
 │                   │  ?checkin=...        │                    │
 │                   │  &checkout=...       │                    │
 │                   │  &adults=2           │                    │
 │                   │  &children=1         │                    │
 │                   │─────────────────────────────────────────→│
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │                   │  { rooms: [{         │                    │
 │                   │    slug, name,       │                    │
 │                   │    available,        │                    │
 │                   │    nightly_rate,     │                    │
 │                   │    total, packages   │                    │
 │                   │  }]}                 │                    │
 │                   │←──────────────────────────────────────────│
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │  Merge: match     │                      │                    │
 │  slug to website  │                      │                    │
 │  content (or use  │                      │                    │
 │  API name),       │                      │                    │
 │  render merged    │                      │                    │
 │  cards            │                      │                    │
 │←──────────────────│                      │                    │
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │  Select room      │                      │                    │
 │──────────────────→│                      │                    │
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │                   │  POST /quote         │                    │
 │                   │  { room_type_id,     │                    │
 │                   │    dates, guests,    │                    │
 │                   │    packages }        │                    │
 │                   │─────────────────────────────────────────→│
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │                   │  { pricing, taxes,   │                    │
 │                   │    packages, total } │                    │
 │                   │←──────────────────────────────────────────│
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │  Show summary     │                      │                    │
 │←──────────────────│                      │                    │
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │  Fill details,    │                      │                    │
 │  Tap "Book"       │                      │                    │
 │──────────────────→│                      │                    │
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │                   │  POST /book          │                    │
 │                   │  { booking details } │                    │
 │                   │─────────────────────────────────────────→│
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │                   │  { confirmation }    │                    │
 │                   │←──────────────────────────────────────────│
 │                   │                      │                    │
 │  Show confirmation│                      │                    │
 │←──────────────────│                      │                    │
API Call Triggers
Trigger API Call  Payload Website Content Used
Page load None (content from website layer) — Room catalogue loaded (text content, presentation* — all optional)
User taps "Check Availability"  GET /availability dates, adults, children, promo code Room cards already rendered with content
User selects a room POST /quote room_type_id, dates, guests, selected packages  Room name displayed from website content (or API fallback)
User changes packages POST /quote updated package selection —
User taps "Complete Booking"  POST /book  room_type_id, dates, guests, packages, guest details  —
User changes dates after selection  Re-call GET /availability then POST /quote  updated params  Room cards re-render with new availability
User changes guest count after selection  Re-call GET /availability then POST /quote  updated params  —
Debouncing & Edge Cases
- Search button: Disable during API call, re-enable on response
- Package toggle: Debounce 300ms before calling /quote
- Date picker: Wait for both dates to be selected before enabling search
- Guest count: Validate max occupancy against room capacity (from website content, if available; otherwise let InnPilot enforce) before allowing selection
- Promo code: Apply on search (part of availability call) or on quote — depends on API design
- Slug mismatch: If API returns a slug not in website content, render with API data only and the compact layout
- Content layer failure: If website content fails to load (CMS unreachable), cards render with API data only. Booking remains functional.
15. Validation Behaviour
Field Validation Rules
Field Rule  Error Message
Check-in  Required, must be today or future "Check-in date is required"
Check-out Required, must be after check-in  "Check-out must be after check-in"
Adults  Required, min 1, max 8  "At least 1 adult is required"
Children  Optional, 0–6 —
First Name  Required, min 2 chars "Please enter your first name"
Last Name Required, min 2 chars "Please enter your last name"
Email Required, valid format  "Please enter a valid email address"
Phone Required, valid format  "Please enter a valid phone number"
Special Requests  Optional, max 500 chars —
Promo Code  Optional, validated by InnPilot API "This code doesn't seem to be valid" (from API)
Validation Timing
- On submit only for guest details (not on blur for every field)
- On blur for email (immediate format check)
- On change for dates (if check-out < check-in, auto-correct or warn)
- Inline errors, not modals
Progressive Disclosure
The guest details section only appears after a room is selected. This prevents the user from seeing a form they can't use yet.
Occupancy Validation
When the user selects guest counts, the frontend checks against the room's max occupancy (from website content, if available). If the guest count exceeds the room's capacity:
- The room card shows a subtle note: "This room accommodates up to X guests" (if occupancy data exists)
- The "Select" button is not disabled (InnPilot may have its own rules)
- InnPilot enforces the actual booking constraint at /book time
- If no occupancy data exists in website content: The check is skipped. InnPilot enforces the constraint.
16. Trust-Building Opportunities
Source: Website Content
All trust signals are website content. They are not fetched from InnPilot. They are part of the website's editorial layer and can be updated independently. All trust signals are progressive enhancements. Their absence does not affect the booking flow.
Placement Strategy
Trust signals are placed at decision points — moments where the user is most likely to hesitate.
Signal  Placement Format  Source  Enhancement Level
Google Reviews (4.9 ★)  Below search bar, above rooms Badge with star icon and count  Website content Enhancement
"Direct Booking Benefits" Below hero, above search  Small text strip  Website content Enhancement
Secure Payment  Booking summary, below CTA  Lock icon + "SSL Encrypted" Website content Enhancement
Free Cancellation Booking summary, below CTA  "Free cancellation up to 48 hours before check-in"  Website content + InnPilot cancellation rules Enhancement (editorial) / Critical (rules)
Best Rate Guarantee Trust strip, below guest details  "We guarantee the best rate when you book direct" Website content Enhancement
Guest Testimonials  Trust strip, below guest details  2–3 short quotes from real guests Website content Enhancement
Wildlife Experiences  Below rooms, before guest details "Your stay includes access to…" Website content Enhancement
Location Advantages Footer CTA section  Distance to park gate, distance to railway  Website content Enhancement
Free Cancellation — Merged Source
"Free Cancellation" is a trust signal that combines both sources:
- Website content provides the marketing copy: "Free cancellation up to 48 hours before check-in"
- InnPilot provides the actual cancellation rules and deadlines
- The frontend displays the website's marketing copy, but links to the API's specific cancellation terms for the selected booking
Trust Strip Design
A horizontal row of 4 trust items, evenly spaced:
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ⭐ 4.9/5       🔒 Secure       ✓ Free Cancel       🏆 Best │
│  47 Google       Payment         Up to 48hrs          Rate   │
│  Reviews         Encrypted       Before              Guarantee│
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
- Subtle background (light cream or white)
- Icons are muted green
- Text is small, uppercase labels
- No clickable links (purely informational)
- Progressive enhancement: If no trust content is defined, the entire strip is omitted. No placeholder.
Testimonial Display
Two to three short guest quotes, displayed as a horizontal scroll or static strip:
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  "The most peaceful place we've ever stayed. The kids   │
│   didn't want to leave."                                │
│   — Priya M., Delhi · Google Reviews                    │
│                                                          │
│  "Booking direct was so much easier than OTA. And the   │
│   safari package was incredible."                        │
│   — Arjun K., Mumbai · Google Reviews                   │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
- Progressive enhancement: If no testimonials exist, the section is omitted. No "Testimonials coming soon" placeholder.
